    "created_at": "2017-12-29T11:48:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-12-29T11:48:27Z",
    "body": "I was mainly thinking about the `oninput` event handler. Currently it uses names, which are only available in the scope of the form. When using IDs it resolves these from the global scope. All other examples with IDs use `document.getElementById` to find the element.\r\n\r\nI don't mind changing the example to only IDs, though. Should I convert the `oninput` handler to use `document.getElementById`, too? Or just use example as I wrote it above?",
